{"id":"86dc97cc-cebb-48c3-a032-96bd63459e79","object":"chat.completion","created":1793334141,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"\n\n```python\nr = read_range(\"deepinfer/logger.py\", 40, 200)\nprint(r[\"content\"])\nprint(search_code(\"envs\", [\"deepinfer/logger.py\"], 10))\n```","reasoning_content":"I need to implement logger.py changes and stats_logger.py. environ.py is already done. Let me write logger.py changes.\n\nCurrent formatter:\n```python\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        fmt: str,\n        datefmt: str | None = None,\n        high_precision: bool = False,\n        use_color: bool = False,\n    ) -> None:\n        super().__init__(fmt, datefmt)\n        self.high_precision = high_precision\n        self.use_color = use_color\n```\n\nNeed to add max_message_chars keyword-only. Wait \"保留原有四个位置参数，新参数 max_message_chars 只能按名称传入\" — keyword-only.\n\nformat: need to truncate record.message after replacing args, without modifying shared record. Approach: compute message ourselves without mutating record. `super().format(record)` uses record.message = record.getMessage(). We can do:\n\n```python\ndef format(self, record):\n    msg = super().format(record)  # record.message set by formatter\n    ...\n```\nTruncating the final message including prefix? Requirement: budget only restricts message body, not prefix/time/level/exceptions. Simplest: build the body first.\n\nApproach in format:\n```python\ndef format(self, record):\n    record.message = record.getMessage()  # this sets attribute on shared record but original behavior does too; fine? \"不能改写共享原记录的 msg、args、exc_info、stack_info\" — message attribute is set by logging.Formatter anyway.\n```\nActually setting record.message is what logging does. Acceptable? The tests probably check msg/args unchanged. But safer: don't mutate at all. Compute body = record.getMessage(); truncate it; then format using a copy? We could use a shallow copy of the record via `logging.makeLogRecord(record.__dict__)` ... hmm.\n\nCleaner: compute the truncated body ourselves, and format with a copy of the record where message is truncated.\n\nLet me implement:\n\n```python\n_TRUNCATE_MARKER = \"...<omitted>...\"\n\ndef _truncate_message(msg: str, max_chars: int) -> str:\n    if len(msg) <= max_chars:\n        return msg\n    remaining = max_chars - len(_TRUNCATE_MARKER)\n    if remaining <= 0:\n        return _TRUNCATE_MARKER[:max_chars]\n    head = (remaining + 1) // 2\n    tail = remaining - head\n    return msg[:head] + _TRUNCATE_MARKER + (msg[-tail:] if tail else \"\")\n```\nCheck example: budget 32, marker length 15 → remaining 17, head = 9, tail = 8. ✓\n\nformat implementation:\n```python\ndef format(self, record):\n    if self.max_message_chars is None or getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", False) is True:\n        return self._format_impl(record)\n    # avoid mutating the shared record\n    msg = record.getMessage()\n    truncated = _truncate_message(msg, self.max_message_chars)\n    if truncated == msg:\n        return self._format_impl(record)\n    record_copy = logging.makeLogRecord(record.__dict__)\n    record_copy.message = truncated\n    record_copy.msg = truncated\n    record_copy.args = ()\n    return self._format_impl(record_copy)\n```\n\nHmm, but `logging.Formatter.format` calls `record.getMessage()` which returns record.msg if no args → so setting msg=truncated and args=() works. Also exc_info will be formatted from record_copy.exc_info — copy shares exc_info so traceback preserved. stack_info preserved. Good.\n\nBut wait: the `formatTime` uses record.created - makeLogRecord copies __dict__ so created copied. `record.msecs` — makeLogRecord copies msecs? LogRecord.__init__ computes msecs but makeLogRecord sets __dict__ directly from dict, so msecs is copied. Good. Also `record.message` set to truncated.\n\nBut careful: record_copy for high precision - msecs copied, ok.\n\nAlso careful: existing code uses `record.message` in multi-line handling: prefix find. With copy, record_copy.message is truncated; the formatted msg will contain that; prefix computed correctly.\n\nHmm, but the original _format_impl uses `record.message` — for the non-truncated path, logging.Formatter.format sets record.message. Fine.\n\nAlso `formatException` uses record.exc_info. Copy ok.\n\nNow potential test: they may check `formatter.format(record)` result contains time prefix and truncated body. Good.\n\nEdge: keep_full_message must be exactly True → `getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", False) is True`.\n\nAlso validation in __init__: max_message_chars None or int >=32, bool not int.\n\n```python\nif max_message_chars is not None:\n    if isinstance(max_message_chars, bool) or not isinstance(max_message_chars, int) or max_message_chars < 32:\n        raise ValueError(f\"max_message_chars must be None or an int >= 32, got {max_message_chars!r}\")\n```\n\nDefault init: pass max_message_chars=envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS. Need import envs. Check logger.py imports: does it import envs? Not in what I saw (lines 1-40 imports don't include envs). But environ imports? environ doesn't import logger. So `from deepinfer import envs` in logger should be fine... unless environ imports logger (no). Let me check the rest of logger.py for existing imports of envs. I saw lines 1-40. Let me read file middle part 40-96 already seen; no envs import. I'll add `from deepinfer import envs` — but careful about circular import: environ imports nothing from deepinfer? It imports os, threading, collections.abc, datetime, typing. Fine.\n\nWait — but there might be an existing import inside logger.py elsewhere, e.g. `from deepinfer.environ import envs`. Let me just check by searching for \"envs\" in logger.py. Also need to see the rest of file (lines 100-end) to know about checkpoint stuff.\n\nAlso `_setup_logger` — \"重复初始化不能重复添加处理器\" already handled via _default_handler is None. It re-creates formatter each call, applying current config. Good.\n\nLet me read the remainder of logger.py and check envs usage."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10183,"completion_tokens":1435,"total_tokens":11618,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":4096},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1388},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":4096,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":6087},"system_fingerprint":"bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}